      question: { q: 'Two releases differ by 10⁻⁵ rad and the separation grows as e^{λt} with λ ≈ 3 s⁻¹. Roughly when are they a full radian apart?', a: 'Solve 10⁻⁵ e^{3t} = 1: t = ln(10⁵)/3 ≈ 11.5/3 ≈ 3.8 s. Making the initial gap 1000 times smaller only adds ln(1000)/3 ≈ 2.3 s.' },
      equations: ['δ(t) ≈ δ₀ e^{λt}', 'λ = (1/t) ln(δ/δ₀)'],
