      h1: 'Lorentz force simulation',
      intro: 'A magnetic field pushes a moving charge sideways, at right angles to both its velocity and the field. The push never speeds the particle up or slows it down; it only bends its path, which is why charges spiral around field lines.',
      see: 'Charged particles move through a uniform magnetic field. Motion across the field bends into circles; any motion along the field carries on unchanged, so the combination is a helix. The force arrow always points to the centre of the circle.',
